From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:13:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3309/3799] soh: rename func_800FC868 ->
 SystemHeap_ConstructArray

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: walks an array of blocks calling the caller's one-argument function on each
Defined in soh/src/code/system_heap.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/system_heap.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/system_heap.c b/soh/src/code/system_heap.c
index ec77ace09..5ba8a6786 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/system_heap.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/system_heap.c
@@ -114,7 +114,8 @@ void SystemHeap_Delete(void* ptr) {
     }
 }
 
-void func_800FC868(void* blk, u32 nBlk, u32 blkSize, arg3_800FC868 arg3) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_800FC868: walks an array of blocks calling the caller's one-argument function on each
+void SystemHeap_ConstructArray(void* blk, u32 nBlk, u32 blkSize, arg3_800FC868 arg3) {
     uintptr_t pos;
 
     for (pos = (uintptr_t)blk; pos < (uintptr_t)blk + (nBlk * blkSize); pos = (uintptr_t)pos + (blkSize & ~0)) {
